01:06:35,720 --> 01:06:51,720
 It's not that they're running ahead. This is how it works. One head yanks the other as they are racing forward. No one's going to solve the privacy problem until there's a product that you want to launch that needs privacy that isn't going to work without it.

443
01:06:51,720 --> 01:07:04,720
 You need to bang your head against the wall and fix that problem. Then vice versa, some products can't take off unless they have privacy built in out the gate and people need to research and push the research ahead to do it.

444
01:07:04,720 --> 01:07:12,720
 I don't think that we're getting too far ahead. There are ways to get little cut set privacy and add incrementally more privacy, and there's a lot of people who think about it.

